WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:04.220
Hello! How do, it me! How you? Good! Great!

00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.360
Ok, this is mostly for audio test.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.160
Not for you, for me.

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.020
Great.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.960
Hi guys! Uh, Mark here.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.080
Just first off the bat, my glasses broke. Hurray!

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:19.440
I wasn't doing anything with them, except running into a wall. Repeatedly.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.780
I had to do that multiple times because I didn't get it right on the first take...

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.520
It looked too fake! I had to make it look real!

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.080
So I had to really slam into that thing!

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.780
And of course I edited it in post, but, that hurt! A LOT!

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:34.900
And I think it might have lead to the destruction of my glasses...

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.720
But either way I was just wearing them yesterday

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:40.900
And they literally fell off of my face in pieces.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:44.340
Like, they just had enough, for the three years that I had these

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.740
uh, particular set of glasses, it was just,

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.420
"ALRIGHT WE'VE HAD ENOUGH OF THIS FUCKO HERE TIME TO GIVE UP ON LIFE!"

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:51.760
Oop, there it goes again.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.880
Sooooo, I no longer have glasses.
For now.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.760
I'm- IT DAT CONTACT BOI, DAT ME!

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.760
Am I memeing hard enough for you guys?

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:06.840
I'm really trying here. So it's gonna be glasses-less Markimoo for the next few weeks. BECAUSE APPARENTLY

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.900
The place that I went to can't make them in house,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.480
And they have to send off, for some strange material

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.120
That they get from space, in order to make the lenses for my glasses,

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.040
Because I have really FUCKED UP eyes.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.000
Because my eyes, if I don't control them they just pop out of my head

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.040
And go wandering off in different directions. Of course that's not true,

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.740
It's an exaggeration, what we in the 'business' call,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.280
HYPERBOLE!

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.460
Or a god damn lie.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:35.420
But back to the crux of this vlog, I wanted to talk about something very specific and near and dear to my heart! Which is,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.900
The topic of stress.

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.660
Because this past week has been a bit of a hell for me!

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.300
I was in DC for a loooong time

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.100
And I was stuck in the airport over and over and over again

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:51.220
And I made a vlog about this that kind of roasted Delta a little bit

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:53.440
Because they really screwed me over

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.040
like, they - it wasn't that like- I get it, their computer systems went down

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.640
But it wasn't that that REALLY screwed me over

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.480
It was that they continually rebooked me on flights

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:06.600
that were then subsequently cancelled!

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.120
I didnt- I KNOW I could've rebooked on another airline

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.120
I could've done that, that would've been easy for me

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.600
but if I had done- they, they PROMISED me that they would go and

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:18.560
I TRUSTED THEM.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.020
WHY?

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.200
I- it's partially my fault because

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.580
I trusted them when obviously they were having horrible computer issues but...

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.820
EVERYONE I TALKED TO WAS SO ADAMANT

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:35.000
that I would be flying home on the next plane, I even patiently waited the first day because I was like

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.600
"OH, IT'S OKAY, I'll hang out with Bob for another day!"

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:41.960
And then by day three, he was SICK OF ME

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:46.160
*laughter* I am not good company to be around for that long!

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.460
So, stress and the lack thereof in my life

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:53.580
because one of the great things that came out of that trip

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.540
besides a charity livestream which was extremely succesful and thank you everyone

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.540
who joined in on that stream

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.980
but the other great thing that came out of that weekend

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.980
was two discoveries of mine

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.440
And they're more re-discoveries more than they are discoveries themselves

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:13.540
but number one: That crap vlog I made? That was one of the most fun videos

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.100
I've done in a long time because

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:22.600
it was just me, Bob, his wife, his brother-in-law and all four of us just going out

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.860
on the town, bringing the camera with us, and just being stupid and having fun

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:33.380
OUT IN THE REAL WORLD with REAL PEOPLE and REAL SUNLIGHT

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:36.140
lots of real stuff out there, it was cool

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:39.160
It was so good to just be able to go out and do stuff, and you know

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.000
and I'm not saying I DISLIKE doing gaming videos

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.280
or even doing this strange vlog that's in my bathroom

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:49.280
that I've been doing and it became a habit of mine and I should probably break it but

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.740
the lighting's so good so I can't really ignore it?

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.420
but it kinda unearthed this potential and I hope to do more stuff like that in the future

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:00.480
I really do- ummm my buddy Tyler is actually moving to LA

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.500
You guys know Tyler.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.420
*sings* No Word Tyler

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.120
Stone-Face Tyler!

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.480
HE HAS NO FACE!!!

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.200
(Eugh shit...)

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:13.180
But my buddy Tyler is moving to LA in just a few weeks

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:17.580
and together I fully intend to go out more and do more stuff

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.360
and even meet fans, because every time I go out now, like someone

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.960
comes up to me and recognises me from my videos

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:27.260
and I'm honoured to meet 'em, and maybe now when people come up to me

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.540
they can be in videos too!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.520
That would be super cool! Like it would be really awesome to be able to go out there,

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:36.740
and meet these people and also have them be featured in these

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:40.600
random stupid vlogs that I do. Like that would be awesome! I would love that.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.080
And that second thing, that I kind of rediscovered,

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.840
about uhh what I love about youtube is doing stupid little sketches

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.160
and the Delta one was

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.560
*smooches fingers*

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.800
I mean actually it was

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.320
*pfft noises*

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:56.600
But in all honesty, it was shot in like no light

00:04:56.600 --> 00:05:00.920
It was done on Bob's little camcorder, with the camcorder audio...

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:03.180
So surprisingly good for what it was,

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:07.940
And then the special- the 'special effects' was just "I hope this works!"

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.940
I have no idea if this is going to blend!

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:15.740
And we just did it and it was fun, we did it in like two hours and it took three hours to edit

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:21.060
and then like- we just ran to CVS to get stupid supplies because we didn't know how to make-

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.580
like a mask that said Delta on it

00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.480
so we just literally got cardboard paper and *laughing* drew Delta on it

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.020
and it was awesome!

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:32.180
And that was fun! It was so fun!

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:33.940
And then lately I've just been- you know-

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:37.040
for fun I've been doing these other stupid crap videos

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.040
and I LOVE IT!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.260
I LOVE IT!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:45.800
OH... I LOVE IT! I love doing these things! I love 'em! Ohhhh! *laughing* I love it

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:47.580
so much!

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:52.220
Oh you guys don't know how much I- how- how- how happy it makes me when I make these videos.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:56.140
And again, I'm not saying I dislike making these gaming videos,

00:05:56.140 --> 00:06:01.660
but, it's like this little bit of passion to let the- let out the stupid IN MY SOUL!

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:06.160
I have to channel it somehow, or else it's gonna build up inside me!

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.720
And turn into rage *giggles*

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:09.940
That's not good...

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.340
So it's fun, and coming back to the topic of stress

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:17.880
is what I'm trying to say is I came out of a very stressful situation

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:21.640
And I turned it into something really creative for myself.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:27.180
So I may have suffered at the hands of forces beyond my control,

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:34.260
But out of it came some really cool things and some cooler things that I think you will like in the future.

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:38.600
It's going to be a fun, fun time going forward, when Tyler gets here

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:43.380
I cannot wait to show you the  stupider side of my brain!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:49.860
*giggling* I can't wait to show you how many stupid ideas we together can make.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.140
And it's going to be 100% awesome

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:57.300
And there's going to be 100% more cool stuff for you guys.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.420
So thank you everybody so much for watching.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:06.260
And as always... I will see you... In the next video! Buh bye!

